Feature: F9 romaneio .31 — the audit's positive regressions (backend x scenario)

  # (B-S1) The own backend coerces into a null-union at EVERY placement that declares a type, not
  # only at the binding: `x = null` after a `T | null` binding used to write a raw `const 0` into the
  # VReg the `match` then reads as the wrapper's base address — a load from address 0. The `c` rows
  # are the differential control: the C backend wrapped at the assign all along.
  Scenario Outline: null_union_reassign_to_null (own-native — o cenario afirma o proprio valor; nao ha mais arco C contra o que diferir)
    Given target = "host"
    Given source = "examples/regressions/cwd_build/cases/<program>.tks"
    When built and run
    Then exit = <exit>

    # `Given target = "host"` is not decoration: the fold keys a group on target-plus-env, and an
    # ABSENT target keys as "" while an explicit one keys as `host` — so without it these two rows
    # opened two groups of their own instead of joining the host groups the rest of the corpus
    # already pays for. Measured: 2 builds became 0.
    Examples:
      | program          | exit |
      | own_differential | 42   |

  # (A-S7, the D1 direction with ZERO coverage before this) A GENUINE boundary cast must stay
  # SILENT: `(a to u64) * b` with u32 operands joins to u32 WITHOUT the cast and to u64 WITH it, so
  # the cast is load-bearing — the pre-fix predicate ignored the partner operand and rejected it,
  # which would have made every width-widening boundary in the corpus uncompilable.


Feature: class layout — a class registers the layout of its effective instance fields

  # The native lowering collected a layout for a `StructBody` only; a `ClassBody` fell through the
  # catch-all arm of `collect_struct_layout_decl` and registered NOTHING, so EVERY class
  # instantiation died at compile time with "no layout registered for struct `…`" — one class in
  # one namespace, with no same-name type anywhere, was enough to trigger it.
  #
  # `class_layout_effective_fields` asserts both halves off one build. The class half: an
  # `abstract` base's fields are the PREFIX of the derived instance (field-flattening composition),
  # so the inherited AND the own fields must each read back the value they were constructed with,
  # and a method summing across the boundary must agree — an overlapping or reordered slot shows up
  # as a wrong exit code, not as a compile error. The struct half is the control: it is the arm
  # that already worked, so a fix that broke it fails HERE instead of passing quietly.
  Scenario: class_layout_effective_fields (own-native — a class instance is a field-shaped object)
    Given target = "host"
    Given source = "examples/regressions/cwd_build/cases/class_layout_effective_fields.tks"
    When built and run
    Then exit = 42
